clear;
clc;

N = 10^6; % Number of bits

rng(100); % Initialize random generator

% Transmitter
ip = rand(1,N) > 0.5; % Random bits

s = 2*ip - 1; % BPSK modulation

% AWGN Noise
n = 1/sqrt(2) * (randn(1,N) + 1i*randn(1,N));

Eb_N0_dB = -3:10;

for ii = 1:length(Eb_N0_dB)

    % Add noise
    y = s + 10^(-Eb_N0_dB(ii)/20) * n;

    % Receiver
    ipHat = real(y) > 0;

    % Count Errors
    nErr(ii) = sum(ip ~= ipHat);

end

% Simulated BER
simBer = nErr / N;

% Theoretical BER
theoryBer = 0.5 * erfc(sqrt(10.^(Eb_N0_dB/10)));

% Plot
figure;

semilogy(Eb_N0_dB, theoryBer, 'b.-');
hold on;

semilogy(Eb_N0_dB, simBer, 'mx-');

grid on;

axis([-3 10 1e-5 0.5]);

legend('Theory', 'Simulation');

xlabel('Eb/No (dB)');
ylabel('Bit Error Rate (BER)');

title('BER Performance of BPSK in AWGN Channel');

Code Explanation (BPSK BER Simulation in AWGN)

1. Clear Previous Data

clear

Clears all previous variables from workspace.


---

2. Number of Bits

N = 10^6;

Generates 10 lakh bits for transmission.


---

3. Random Generator Initialization

rng(100);

Initializes random generator for same output every run.


---

4. Generate Random Bits

ip = rand(1,N) > 0.5;

Creates random binary bits:

1 if value > 0.5

0 otherwise



---

5. BPSK Modulation

s = 2*ip - 1;

Converts bits into BPSK symbols:

1 → +1

0 → -1



---

BPSK Formula

s = 2b - 1


---

6. AWGN Noise Generation

n = 1/sqrt(2)*(randn(1,N) + 1i*randn(1,N));

Generates Gaussian noise for channel.


---

7. Eb/N0 Range

Eb_N0_dB = -3:10;

Signal-to-noise ratio varies from -3 dB to 10 dB.


---

8. Add Noise

y = s + 10^(-Eb_N0_dB(ii)/20)*n;

Adds noise to transmitted signal.


---

9. Receiver Decision

ipHat = real(y) > 0;

Receiver checks:

Positive → 1

Negative → 0



---

10. Count Errors

nErr(ii) = sum(ip ~= ipHat);

Counts incorrect bits.


---

11. BER Calculation

simBer = nErr / N;

Calculates simulated Bit Error Rate.


---

12. Theoretical BER

theoryBer = 0.5 * erfc(sqrt(10.^(Eb_N0_dB/10)));

Computes theoretical BER for BPSK.


---

BER Formula

P_b = \frac{1}{2}\operatorname{erfc}\left(\sqrt{\frac{E_b}{N_0}}\right)


---

13. Plotting

semilogy(Eb_N0_dB, theoryBer)

Plots BER vs Eb/N0 graph on logarithmic scale.


